🟩 Ultra‑Minimal Recovery Cheat Sheet 
Linksys E4200v2 / EA4500 (Viper)
Code
=================  E4200v2 / EA4500 QUICK RECOVERY  =================

1. SERIAL SETUP
   - 115200 8N1, 3.3V logic
   - Connect GND – TX – RX
   - Open terminal BEFORE powering router

2. ENTER U-BOOT
   - Power on
   - Interrupt at: "Hit any key to stop autoboot:"
   - Prompt: Viper>>

3. SET TFTP
   setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.10
   setenv serverip 192.168.1.2

4. LOAD FIRMWARE TO RAM
   tftpboot 0x800000 ea4500.bin
   (Note hex size, e.g. 0x880000)

5. ERASE NAND
   nand erase 0x200000 0x1e00000

6. WRITE FIRMWARE
   nand write 0x800000 0x200000 <hex_size>

7. IMPORTANT: (DO NOT USE "reset") Or (Use Reset) 
---
   - Router "May" freeze (solid LED) — this is normal in some cases, which makes it abnormal in others.
I have carried ou this procedure more than once, and in some cases the rest works from within Putty
and in other cases it does not and the router hangs. I cannot definitely state why, however i have overcome the issue by just simply unplugging the router
and plugging it back in after approx 10 seconds or so, who's counting maybe it was 20. Upon restart it ran normally,
Luci was accessable at 192.168.1.1 and putty showed all the correct codes on the screen. 
---

8. HARD POWER CYCLE
   - Unplug power
   - Wait 5–10 seconds
   - Plug back in

9. SUCCESSFUL BOOT
   - Look for: "Starting kernel ..."
   - OpenWrt at 192.168.1.1 (root / no password)

